# Deny by default.
#
# The build context for drill/Containerfile is the REPO ROOT, because the grader
# reads scenarios/answers/*.toml at runtime and those live above drill/. That puts
# scripts/config.toml - AWS account id, profile name, your public IP - and
# .kubeconfig-daily-eks-practice inside the context of an image published PUBLICLY.
#
# So this is an allow-list, not an exclude-list. An exclude-list leaks the next
# secret file somebody adds and says nothing when it does; an allow-list cannot.
# Only these two trees have any business in the image.
#
# Adding a `!` line here is a security decision. tests/test_containerignore.py fails
# the static suite if one of them would re-admit scripts/, terraform/ or a kubeconfig,
# and the built-image assertion in plan Task 5.5 Step 4 checks the result rather than
# the intent.
*
!drill/
!scenarios/answers/

# ...minus the parts of drill/ that must not be in it either. node_modules is a HOST
# build - glibc or musl depending on who ran it, and node-pty is native - and copying
# it in would shadow the one `npm ci` builds inside the image. dist/ is stale output
# for the same reason.
drill/node_modules/
drill/*/node_modules/
drill/*/dist/
drill/**/*.tsbuildinfo
